From 969d880cdbb5fd5e5b920f550ff3bf7e28a7fa91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:54:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): close scratch custody gaps (archived
 rows, Board-claim receipts, preserve list)

Worker-2 kept stranding scratch trees that no pass could ever reclaim
(t_01a1d66ffbda6276, 67.7 GiB):

1. _terminal accepts a Board row with status='archived' and
   completed_at null. Its retention clock is the newest of the row's
   updated_at (ms) and the latest ended run on the receipt. Live row,
   uid match and expired lease are still required, and 'done' still
   needs completed_at. Callers age trees by owner["retention_at"].
2. New kanban_scratch_custody_discovery: for a root child named
   exactly t_[0-9a-f]{16} that is a plain managed-scratch dir with no
   local row (any board) and no receipt, it reads the Board and writes
   a {"kind":"board","runs":[...]} receipt only when:
   - the Board row is workspace_kind='scratch';
   - a Board 'claimed' event's lock starts with this host's
     hostname_prefix;
   - every such claim's run has ended.
   Discovery never deletes. Removal stays the unchanged gc_custody
   path. A Board error, a missing row or a missing replica leaves the
   tree owner_unverified.
3. retain() records the default <root>/<id> tree when a scratch row's
   workspace_path is NULL, if that dir exists.
4. kanban.scratch_gc_preserve (unset = []; documented, not in
   config_defaults to respect its line cap) lists task ids that no
   scratch removal path touches. It is enforced in
   defer_owned_job_cleanup (completion and deferred cleanup, custody
   GC, the disk-pressure adapter), in the retention GC walk, in the
   custody receipt loop and in discovery. A tree is pinned when any
   path component is a listed id. A malformed or unreadable setting
   pins every tree.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_scratch_custody_gaps.py (58). On
base plus the two new standalone modules, 15 fail across all four
items; on this head all pass, and the scratch/worker-node/jobs
regression set passes 509/509.
